    {
      "id": 202476,
      "name": "Phantom5613",
      "username": "Phantom5613",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-08-28T21:59:50.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The 2001-2002 Tick that starred Patrick Warburton(sp?) was certainly a fun comedy show, but behind the scenes there were quite a few problems with schedueling and funding. I believe the team did the best that they could with what they had, and I loved it, but unfortunatly it wasn't as good of a show that it could have been if it had the right resources. I'd like to think this new&nbsp;show is what we could have gotten if the stars alligned and The Tick got the funds and time it needed.</p><p>Comedy was more the focus than super heroics for the 2000's show(due to not having the budget for many special effects), but with this new series we're able to get both humor AND heroics!</p><p>I urge any Tick fan, young or old, to give the amazon show a try.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:31:14.333Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
